= Inserting the Cartridge

Connect your ARCADIA-2001 to the television as its own Owner’s Manual shows:
the output cable into the antenna switch box, the switch box at *GAME*, and
the television on channel 3 or 4, whichever the switch on the back of the
console is set to.

#fig-rear

#fig-insert

== Operation

#steps(
  [Be sure the *POWER* switch is in OFF position (red POWER light OFF).],
  [Hold the FujiNet cartridge so the label faces you and reads right side up,
   the contacts down.],
  [Insert the cartridge into the cartridge slot, firmly but do not force it.
   The top edge, with its USB-C socket, stays standing out of the slot.],
  [Turn on the television and set its volume to a comfortable level.],
  [Press the *POWER* switch to ON. The red light glows, and the FujiNet CONFIG
   appears.],
)

#caution[Be sure the POWER light is off before the cartridge is inserted or
removed. To remove it, just pull straight up.]

The FujiNet CONFIG is worked with the *left* hand controller. Its first
screen comes up in a moment; the first time, it asks for your WiFi network
(Section 6).

== Extra Power

#grid(columns: (2.0in, 1fr), column-gutter: 0.25in, align: (center + top, left + top),
  fig-power,
  [
    The cartridge can run on power from the console, but its WiFi radio needs
    a good deal more, in short bursts, than the games it replaces: a quarter
    to two-thirds again of what the whole console draws. The ARCADIA-2001’s
    AC adaptor was never meant to supply that.

    A *USB-C phone charger* plugged into the top of the cartridge supplies it
    instead. The cartridge takes what it needs from the charger first and
    never sends any of it back to the console. We recommend one whenever you
    play.
  ],
)

#important[Plug the charger into the cartridge *before* you turn the console
on, so the cartridge is already awake when the console first looks at it.]

With a charger plugged in, FujiNet stays awake and connected while the
console is off, so it is ready again the moment you turn the console back on
-- with the game it last loaded still in it (Section 5 tells how to get back
to CONFIG).
